WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.160
Let's get into exactly how chest compressions are done.

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.320
Everything starts with your hands.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.840
Look at the screen and watch your instructor,

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.800
because getting your hand placement right

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:12.800
is the foundation of high-quality CPR.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.639
First, you want to find the center of the person's chest.

00:00:16.639 --> 00:00:19.080
You are going to place the heel of one hand

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.120
directly on the lower half of the breastbone,

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.840
which is also called the sternum.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.000
This is the strongest part of the chest,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.360
and it is right where the heart

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.480
is waiting for that manual pump.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.680
Next, take your other hand and place the heel of it

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.840
right on top of the first one.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.439
From there, lace your fingers together.

00:00:38.439 --> 00:00:41.160
Lacing your fingers helps keep your hands focused

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:44.040
on that center spot so they do not slide around

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.240
while you are working.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:48.040
The final part of your setup is your posture.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:51.520
You need to keep your arms straight and lock your elbows.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.400
Position yourself so your shoulders

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.639
are directly over your hands.

00:00:55.639 --> 00:00:57.959
By doing this, you are not just using

00:00:57.959 --> 00:00:59.799
your arm muscles to push,

00:00:59.799 --> 00:01:03.160
you are using your entire upper body weight to do the work.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:06.559
It is much more effective and less tiring for you.

00:01:06.559 --> 00:01:08.919
Take a moment now to get into this position

00:01:08.919 --> 00:01:10.400
over your mannequin.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.559
Feel that alignment from your shoulders

00:01:12.559 --> 00:01:15.400
all the way down to the heel of your hand.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:16.760
Once you have that locked in,

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.559
we are ready to move on to the actual push.

